This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
freenode.net. Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.

[1]: Random forests, like in the Ranger quest. --SomeoneElseYes

[2]: Satchel of magic seeds; applying plants a seed in the specified
direction which instantly grows into a tree on ground, a water lily on
water and nothing on ice/lava. (Water lillies are terrain that counts
as ground but turns into water if burned/rotted/destroyed somehow/dug
through.) When cursed will produce a single random fruit instead.
--Patashu

[3]: Falling rock traps should be hallucinated as thwomp traps. "A
thwomp falls on your head! THWOMP! Fortunately, you are wearing a hard
helmet." No change in damage or effect or anything. (It can't be a real
trap since it would do nothing at all besides damage, after all)
--Patashu

[4]: Wind trap. Apon activation, your wielded weapon and any items on
the square are tossed upward and fall onto your head. "A sudden gale
blows upward!" (Perhaps toss lightweight items from your inventory
around too? But never into water/lava, that would be terribly
annoying.) --Patashu

[5]: Zapping a wand of nothing at intelligent monsters should scare
them for a turn or two --Botje

[6]: make cows and sheeps etc. --Zaba_

[7]: Yellow dragon scale mail should give petrification-resitance, like
the dragon has. --SomeoneElseYes

[8]: Tourists #chatting with monsters can get directions
(clairvoyance). Need to find a way of giving POOR directions from
chaotic monsters though... --mathx

[9]: copper and silver coins in addition to gold --Zaba_

[10]: Ghosts' strength should reflect the character's level!
--Chilliwack

[11]: A new monster, a trojan horse. Susceptible to rotting like a wood
golem, fairly fast, huge and hits harder then a war horse. Can summon
soldiers around it. Deathdrops quarterstaves and clubs. Possibly follow
up with an iron horse monster at higher levels. --Patashu

[12]: Ice boxes should have a chance of holding potions of booze or
fruit juice in addition to the random corpses. --Patashu

[13]: Eating a banana should leave a banana peel in your inventory.
When dropped and stepped on (by you or a monster) you are sent one tile
in a random direction (the peel slipping the other way) and stunned for
a while. --Patashu

[14]: Bolts of cold should freeze fountains. --BenUrban

[15]: In some cases you might encounter the Fellowship of the Ring. The
members will be generated with artifacts if they do not already exist
in the game, and will either be peaceful, in which case they will
travel to the nearest staircase and disappear, or hostile, in which
case you should leave the level as soon as possible. --TheShrewdDude

[16]: An optional game ending: Rather than giving the Amulet to your
god, you can instead opt to travel to ancient Yendor, which opens up a
whole new realm of possibilities. Which are endless. --TheShrewdDude

[17]: If your luck is in the negative, rooms are generated dark far
more often. --Patashu

[18]: ...and levels, in the Mines. --BenUrban

[19]: Messages should be printed when a monster's teleportitis kicks
in. "The wood nymph steals a blessed rustproof +4 helm of brilliance!"
"The wood nymph giggles and vanishes." No real effect, just flavour.
--Patashu

[20]: Kicking stairs while hallucinating should have a rare (say,
1/256) chance of flipping them over to point up instead of down and
down instead of up. The corrosponding staircase on the level would flip
similarly. --Patashu

[21]: The big room should be generated with randomly scattered trees
and either a lake or a river. Upon entering "This looks like a good
place to have a picnic!" --Patashu

[22]: Rocs, thunderbirds and phoenixes. Because avians are cool. (Rocs
are huge fast flying creatures, thunderbirds are similar only slightly
more powerful and with lightning breath (confers shock resistance when
eaten), phoenixes are slightly more powerful again and with fire
breath, will be resurrected as per an "oLS once and have a tiny chance
of conferring intristic life saving) --Patashu

[23]: Phoenix ashes are left after the death of a phoenix. They will
spontaneously respawn (like trolls) in bursts of flame. You can also
find creative uses for the ashes, such as snorting them or rubbing them
on sores. --TheShrewdDude_


Individual ideas may have contributions from multiple authors/editors,
